### Create account for Alice with initial deposit
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "owner": "Alice",
  "initialDeposit": 1000.00
}

###

### Create account for Bob (no initial deposit)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "owner": "Bob",
  "initialDeposit": 0
}

###

### List all accounts
GET http://localhost:5000/api/accounts

###

### Get account by ID (replace with actual ID from create response)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

###

### Deposit $500 into Alice's account
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/deposit
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "ALICE_ACCOUNT_ID",
  "amount": 500.00
}

###

### Withdraw $200 from Alice's account
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "ALICE_ACCOUNT_ID",
  "amount": 200.00
}

###

### Transfer $300 from Alice to Bob
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountId": "ALICE_ACCOUNT_ID",
  "toAccountId": "BOB_ACCOUNT_ID",
  "amount": 300.00
}

###

### Undo the last command (reverses the transfer)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/undo

###

### Redo the last undone command (re-applies the transfer)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/redo

###

### Undo again — should fail (nothing to undo after redo + new commands cleared stack)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/undo

###

### View full command execution history
GET http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/history

###

### Attempt to withdraw more than balance (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/accounts/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "ALICE_ACCOUNT_ID",
  "amount": 999999.00
}
